  - Images: Various historic and modern sites along the route.

- Cabrillo National Monument (code: cabr)
  - States: CA | URL: https://www.nps.gov/cabr/index.htm | Designation: National Monument
  - Description: Commemorates Juan Rodriguez Cabrillo’s 1542 landing (first European on U.S. West Coast); rich cultural/natural resources on Point Loma.
  - Activities: Biking/road biking; hiking; living history/re-enactments/historic weapons demos/first-person interpretation; Junior Ranger; wildlife/birdwatching; park film; museum; shopping/bookstore/gifts.
  - Weather: Mild, semi-arid San Diego climate; warm, dry summers; mild winters; most rain Dec–Mar; ~201 days >70°F; 9–13 inches annual rainfall.
