Tool `National Parks:getParkDetails` with Parameter {'parkCode': 'yose'} on National Parks succeeded. Result (summarized from 3057 tokens): Yosemite National Park (code: yose)
- URL: https://www.nps.gov/yose/index.htm
- Designation: National Park
- State(s): CA

Description
- A celebrated High Sierra landscape known for waterfalls, granite, glaciers, meadows, deep valleys, ancient giant sequoias, and vast wilderness across nearly 1,200 square miles. First protected in 1864.

Weather and Climate
- Area: ~1,200 sq mi (3,100 sq km) in the Sierra Nevada
- Elevation: ~2,000–13,000 ft (600–4,000 m)
- Precipitation: ~95% Oct–May (over 75% Nov–Mar)
- Snow: Most of the park snow-covered Nov–May; Yosemite Valley can be rainy or snowy during winter storms.

Directions
- Year-round vehicle access via Highways 41, 140, and 120 from the west.
- Tioga Pass Entrance (Hwy 120 from the east): typically closed approximately Nov through late May or June.
- Hetch Hetchy: open year-round but may close intermittently due to snow; road closed to all vehicles from sunset to sunrise (except permitted backpackers in area during open times).
- GPS may be inaccurate for routes to/within the park.
- Driving info: http://www.nps.gov/yose/planyourvisit/driving.htm

Location
- Latitude: 37.84883288; Longitude: -119.5571873
- Mailing address: PO Box 577, Yosemite National Park, CA 95389

Contacts
- Phone: 209/372-0200
- Email: yose_web_manager@nps.gov

Entrance Fees (valid 7 consecutive days unless noted)
- Entrance - Private Vehicle: $35.00; covers a non-commercial car/pickup/RV/van (≤15 passengers) and all occupants.
- Entrance - Motorcycle: $30.00; per motorcycle.
- Entrance - Per Person: $20.00; for entry on foot, bicycle, horse, or non-commercial bus/van; age 15 and under free.
- Commercial Entrance - Sedan: $25.00 + $20.00 per person, not to exceed $105.00; commercial use authorization required.
- Commercial Entrance - Van: $125.00; commercial use authorization required.
- Commercial Entrance - Mini-bus: $200.00; commercial use authorization required.
- Commercial Entrance - Motor Coach: $300.00; commercial use authorization required.
- Entrance - Non-commercial Groups: $20.00 per person up to $300.00 per vehicle; age 15 and under free.
- Entrance - Education/Academic Groups: $0.00 with approved educational fee waiver (for accredited/tax-exempt groups on educational/scientific trips not primarily recreational).
- Commercial Entrance - Per Person: $20.00; plus $25.00 base fee, not to exceed $105.00; commercial use authorization required.

Entrance Passes
- Annual Entrance - Park: $70.00; free entrance to Yosemite for 12 months from purchase.

Operating Hours
- Yosemite National Park: Open 24 hours/day, 365 days/year.
- Hetch Hetchy: Open sunrise to sunset for day use; all day visitors must exit by sunset; road closed to all vehicles from sunset to sunrise (except permitted backpackers during open hours).

Topics
- Architecture and Building; African American Heritage; Archeology; Arts; Painting; Photography; Asian American Heritage; Burial, Cemetery and Gravesite; Native American Heritage; Religion and Spirituality; Churches; Schools and Education; Science, Technology and Innovation; Transportation; Tragic Events; Floods; Women’s History; Animals; Birds; Cats (wild); Fish; Climate Change; Fire; Foothills, Plains and Valleys; Forests and Woodlands; Geology; Glaciers; Grasslands; Meadows; Lakes; Mountains; Natural Sounds; Night Sky; Astronomy; River and Riparian; Rock Landscapes and Features; Scenic Views; Trails; Unique Species; Watersheds; Waterfalls; Wetlands; Wilderness.

Activities
