General
- Weather: Most precipitation Oct–May; much of park snow-covered Nov–May. Check forecast: https://www.nps.gov/yose/planyourvisit/weathermap.htm
- Bears: Proper food storage required; bear lockers provided. Regulations: https://www.nps.gov/yose/planyourvisit/campregs.htm
- Fire rules often restrict wood fires to 5–10 pm May–Sept in Yosemite Valley; charcoal typically allowed anytime.

Bridalveil Creek Campground (Glacier Point Road)
- Location/elevation: Forest of red fir/lodgepole pine near Bridalveil Creek; 7,200 ft; 7 mi W of Glacier Point, 9 mi E of Wawona Road turnoff; ~45 min from Yosemite Valley; no services nearby. 37.6636576, -119.6242934
- Season/reservations: Typically mid-July–early Sept; reservations required for all sites; released 14 days in advance at 7 am PT; book up within minutes. Reserve: https://www.recreation.gov/camping/campgrounds/232453
- Fees/night: $36 (non-group); $75 (group); $50 (stock/horse).
- Capacity/sites: 115 total; 0 FCFS. Types: 2 group, 3 horse, 41 tent-only, 0 electric. Max per site: 6 people (group: 13–30). Vehicles: 2 per site; trailers don’t count if they fit on pad.
- Vehicles: RVs allowed to 35 ft; trailers to 24 ft; paved access.
- Pets/fires: Pets permitted (not in group sites); wood/charcoal fires permitted.
- Amenities: Flush toilets (seasonal), potable water (seasonal), food lockers, dump station, camp store, host onsite, trash/recycling, cell reception, firewood/ice for sale; no showers.
- Accessibility: No designated accessible sites.
- Info: https://www.nps.gov/yose/planyourvisit/bvcamp.htm; Phone: 209-375-9535; Email: yose_web_manager@nps.gov

Camp 4 (Yosemite Valley, near Yosemite Falls)
- Location/elevation: Base of granite cliffs near Yosemite Falls; 4,000 ft; walk/bike to many valley services; near free shuttle; food nearby at Yosemite Valley Lodge and Yosemite Village. 37.7420541, -119.6022531
- Season/reservations: Open year-round. 2025: Apr 18–Nov 15 reservations required, released 1 week in advance; rest of year first-come, self-register. Sites shared; space assigned per person (up to 6 per site). Reserve: https://www.recreation.gov/camping/campgrounds/10004152
- Fees: $10 per person, per night.
- Capacity/sites: 61 tent-only (walk-in); some FCFS period-dependent. Max 6 people per site.
- Vehicles: No RVs/trailers.
- Pets/fires: Pets not permitted. Wood fires allowed year-round but in Valley May–Sept only 5–10 pm; charcoal anytime; air quality may be unhealthy at night.
- Amenities: Flush toilets and potable water year-round, food lockers, trash/recycling, host onsite, camp store nearby, dump station nearby, cell/internet; no showers.
- Accessibility: 2 accessible sites; accessible parking/path; accessible restrooms.
- Info: https://www.nps.gov/yose/planyourvisit/camp4.htm; Phone: 209-372-8502; Email: yose_web_manager@nps.gov

Crane Flat Campground (near Crane Flat)
