Tool `National Parks:getParkDetails` with Parameter {'parkCode': 'seki'} on National Parks succeeded. Result (summarized from 2778 tokens): Sequoia & Kings Canyon National Parks (code: seki)
- Designation: National Parks
- State: CA
- Website: https://www.nps.gov/seki/index.htm

Overview
- Iconic features: world’s largest trees (giant sequoias), huge mountains, rugged foothills, deep canyons, vast caverns; rich biodiversity and scenic variety.
- Conservation note: Ancient giant sequoias, though massive, are vulnerable and face threats.

Weather
- Extreme elevation range creates wide variability.
- Summer: comfortable in sequoia groves; foothills hot/dry; snow lingers on high passes.
- Fall: ranges from summer-like to winter-like.
- Winter: snow in sequoia groves, rain in foothills; tire chains often required.
- Spring: ideal for foothill hikes; snowmelt begins at higher elevations.

Directions
- Entrances:
  - Hwy 180 (from Fresno): to Kings Canyon NP; continues 30 miles east to Cedar Grove.
  - Hwy 198 (from Visalia via Three Rivers): to Sequoia NP.
- Inside parks: Hwy 198 becomes Generals Highway, connecting 198 and 180.
- Restrictions/seasonal:
  - Vehicles over 22 feet should enter via Hwy 180.
  - Generals Highway between the parks often closes in winter.
  - Chains may be required on park roads.
  - No roads cross the parks east–west.
- Directions info: http://www.nps.gov/seki/planyourvisit/directions.htm

Location
- Address: 47050 Generals Highway, Three Rivers, CA 93271
- Coordinates: 36.71277299, -118.587429

Contacts
- Phone (voice): 5595653341
- Fax: 5595653730
- Email: SEKI_information@nps.gov

Fees and Passes
- Entrance (valid 1–7 days; also includes Hume Lake District of Sequoia NF/Giant Sequoia NM):
  - Private Vehicle: $35
  - Per Person (on foot/bicycle): $20
  - Motorcycle: $30
- Non-commercial groups:
  - Vehicles up to 15-passenger capacity: $35 per vehicle or use a pass.
  - Vehicles with 16+ capacity: $20 per person, capped at commercial maximums ($100 or $200, see below).
  - Exempt: age 15 and under; anyone with an applicable pass; hired drivers transporting only.
- Commercial tours (fee based on seating capacity; passenger ages/passes do not change price):
  - Sedan (1–6 seats): $25 per vehicle + $20 per passenger; max $75.
  - Per Person (for 1–6 seat vehicles): $20 per person + $25 per vehicle; max $75.
  - Van (7–15 seats): $75
  - Mini-bus (16–25 seats): $100
  - Motor Coach (26+ seats): $200
- Annual Park Pass: $70 (valid for Sequoia & Kings Canyon NPs and Hume Lake Ranger District for 1 year from purchase month; admits all passengers in one private vehicle; non-transferable)

Operating Hours
- Open 24 hours/day, 365 days/year.
- Some roads (especially to remote areas) close in winter due to snow; rare extreme weather may close roads into the parks.

Topics (highlights)
- History & Culture: African American Heritage; Arts (Painting, Photography, Poetry/Literature); Transportation (Roads, Routes, Highways).
- Nature/Science: Animals (Birds), Unique/Rare/Endangered species; Caves/Caverns/Karst; Canyons; Climate Change; Fire; Foothills/Plains/Valleys; Forests/Woodlands (Coniferous); Geology; Grasslands; Meadows; Lakes; Mountains; Natural Sounds; Night Sky/Astronomy; Rivers/Riparian; Rock Landscapes/Features; Scenic Views; Trails; Watersheds/Headwaters; Wilderness.

