Foothills Visitor Center (Sequoia NP)
- Location: 1 mile east/north of Ash Mountain Entrance on Generals Highway. Address: 47050 Generals Highway, Three Rivers, CA 93271.
- Services: Info, maps, books, gifts, water, restrooms; exhibits on foothills ecology and human history. Self-issue wilderness permits outside Wilderness Office (non-quota season).
- Season/hours: Open year-round except weather/emergency/operational closures; hours vary. Typical hours: daily 8:00 AM–5:00 PM.

Giant Forest Museum (Sequoia NP)
- Location: Historic market building in Giant Forest sequoia grove; Generals Highway, 16 miles north of Ash Mountain Entrance. Address: Mile 16, Generals Highway, Sequoia National Park, CA 93262. Elevation: 6,500 ft (1,980 m).
- Services: Info, maps, books, gifts, water, restrooms; hands-on exhibits on giant sequoia ecology. Self-issue wilderness permits in museum plaza (non-quota season).
- Season/hours: Open year-round except weather/emergency/operational closures; hours may vary. Typical hours: daily 9:00 AM–6:00 PM.

Kings Canyon Visitor Center (Grant Grove Village)
- Location: Grant Grove Village on Hwy 180, ~3 miles east of Big Stump Entrance. Address: 83918 Highway 180, Kings Canyon National Park, CA 93633. Elevation: 6,500 ft (1,980 m).
- Services: Maps, info, books, gifts, water, restrooms; exhibits on giant sequoias, Kings Canyon, High Sierra; short park film (English & Spanish). Self-issue wilderness permits at permit station in plaza (non-quota season).
- Season/hours: Open year-round except weather/emergency/other closures; dates/hours may vary. Typical hours: daily 8:00 AM–5:00 PM.

Lodgepole Visitor Center (Sequoia NP)
- Location: Generals Highway, 21 miles north of Ash Mountain Entrance; 2 miles north of General Sherman Tree. Address: 63100 Lodgepole Rd., Sequoia National Park, CA 93262. Elevation: 6,700 ft (2,040 m). Renovated in 2023.
- Services: Info, wilderness permits, park films, maps, books, gifts, water, restrooms; immersive exhibits on diverse ecosystems and human history.
- Season/hours: Summer only, late May/early Jun through late Sep/mid-Oct; hours may vary. Typical hours: daily 8:00 AM–5:00 PM.

Mineral King Ranger Station (Sequoia NP)
- Location: Mineral King Road, 24 miles from Hwy 198 junction in Three Rivers. Address: Mile 24, Mineral King Road, Sequoia National Park, CA 93271. Elevation: 7,600 ft (2,320 m).
- Services: Exhibits on Mineral King human/natural history; books, maps, educational items for sale; food storage canisters available; wilderness permits issued.
- Safety note: If parking overnight, marmots may enter undercarriage or damage wiring—wrap underside of vehicle with a tarp.
- Season/hours: Generally open Memorial Day Weekend–Labor Day Weekend; hours may vary. Typical hours: dail
