- Official site: https://www.nps.gov/jotr/index.htm
- Designation: National Park; State: CA
- Description: Where the Mojave and Colorado Deserts meet, with diverse plants and animals, dark night skies, rich cultural history, and striking geologic features across a vast Southern California wilderness.
- Weather: Typically clear, <25% humidity. Best in spring/fall (avg highs ~85°F/29°C, lows ~50°F/10°C). Winter ~60°F/15°C days, freezing nights; occasional snow at higher elevations. Summer is very hot: >100°F/38°C days, nights ~75°F/24°C+.
- Directions: From I-10, exit 117 to CA-62 for West Entrance, North Entrance, Black Rock, Indian Cove. From I-10, exit 168 for South Entrance. Details: http://www.nps.gov/jotr/planyourvisit/directions.htm
- Location:
  - Coordinates: 33.91418525, -115.8398125
  - Address: 74485 National Park Drive, Twentynine Palms, CA 92277-3597
