Tool `National Parks:getCampgrounds` with Parameter {'parkCode': 'jotr', 'limit': 50} on National Parks succeeded. Result (summarized from 27847 tokens): Joshua Tree National Park – Campground Summary (data provided for 5 of 9 campgrounds)

Park-wide basics
- Operating hours: Campgrounds open 24 hours daily; check-in/out at noon. Quiet hours 10 pm–6 am.
- Weather: Clear, <25% humidity. Spring/fall avg high/low ~85/50°F (29/10°C). Winter ~60°F days with freezing nights; occasional snow at higher elevations. Summer often >100°F days, ~75°F nights. Weather can change quickly—check forecasts.
- Standard site occupancy: Max 6 people, 3 tents, 2 cars per site (only if space allows; some sites fit 1 vehicle).
- General regulations: Pay camping fees within 1 hour of selecting a site (FCFS areas). 30-night limit per year; only 14 nights allowed Oct–May. Set up all gear within 25 ft (7.6 m) of picnic table/fire grate. Secure all food and scented items (incl. sunscreen/toiletries) from wildlife. Sites vacant 24 hours are considered available. No holding sites for others. Pets on leash at all times; may not be left unattended. No slacklines in campgrounds.
- Accessibility notes: ADA campsites are available at Indian Cove (site 1), Jumbo Rocks (site 122), and Black Rock (site 61). Many other sites/roads have uneven terrain.

Campgrounds

1) Belle Campground (18 sites; first-come, first-served year-round)
- Location: Pinto Basin Road near Twentynine Palms, CA 92277.
- How FCFS works: Find an empty site, occupy it, then immediately go to an entrance station to register and pay (within 1 hour). If arriving after stations close, pay in the morning.
- Fees: $25/site; Senior/Access Pass: $12.50.
- Amenities: Vault toilets, picnic tables, fire pits. No water—bring plenty.
- Roads/rigs: Unpaved access roads (OK for all vehicles in good weather). RVs allowed up to 35 ft. Trailers not allowed (no trailer length listed).
- Accessibility: Unpaved/uneven campsites and roads; paved, flat path to bathroom but unpaved road to that path. No ADA-designated sites here.

2) Black Rock Campground (99 sites; reservations required year-round)
- Location: 9800 Black Rock Cyn, Yucca Valley, CA 92284. On the NW corner of the park; 5 miles from Yucca Valley (shopping).
- Reservations: Recreation.gov or 877-444-6777 (book up to 6 months ahead).
- Fees: $35/site (tents, RVs, equestrian); Senior/Access: $17.50. Horse camp: $35 (20 sites; Senior/Access $17.50).
- Amenities: Potable water (year-round), flush toilets, picnic table & fire ring at each site; dump station, day-use picnic area. Separate horse-camping/staging area.
- Roads/rigs: Paved roads (some pavement crumbling); some unpaved roads. RVs up to 35 ft. Trailer details vary (ADA site info below).
- Seasonal: Some sites close in summer.
- Accessibility: Uneven terrain at many sites; wheelchair-accessible restroom at Black Rock Nature Center (parking lot paved/flat). ADA site: Black Rock #61 (back-in), accommodates RV up to 30 ft; trailers + tow vehicle allowed up to 30 ft combined (at that site).

3) Cottonwood Campground (62 sites; reservations required year-round)
- Location: Near Cottonwood Visitor Center, SE park; Indio ~30 miles away. Address: Cottonwood Campground, Pinto Basin Road, Cottonwood Springs, CA 92277.
- Reservations: Recreation.gov or 877-444-6777 (up to 6 months).
- Fees: Individual $35; Group (3 group sites; tents only) $55; Senior/Access: $17.50 (individual), $27.50 (group). Note: Fees increase to $35 (individual) and $55 (group) starting Jan 1, 2025 (already reflected above).
- Amenities: Potable water (year-round), flush toilets; dump station; amphitheater.
- Roads/rigs: Paved access roads; RVs and trailers allowed up to 35 ft.
- Seasonal note: In summer, Loop B typically closes and Loop A usually becomes first-come, first-served (even though general guidance states reservations are required year-round).
- Weather nuance: At ~3,000 ft, typically 5–10°F warmer than the northern park; summer frequently >100°F; winter days ~60°F; subfreezing nights possible.
- Accessibility: No ADA-designated campsites; Cottonwood Amphitheater ADA-accessible f
