- URL: https://www.nps.gov/lavo/index.htm
- Designation: National Park
- State: CA
- Description: Park of steaming fumaroles, wildflower meadows, clear mountain lakes, and numerous volcanoes. Jagged peaks reflect an eruptive past; hot water continues to shape the land.

Location
- Coordinates: 40.49354575, -121.4075993
- Address: 38050 Highway 36 East, Park Headquarters, Mineral, CA 96063

Contact
- Phone: 530-595-6100 (Voice)
- Email: lavo_information@nps.gov

Weather
- Highly variable year-round.
- January avg: high 40.4 °F (4.7 °C), low 20.8 °F (-6.2 °C).
- July avg: high 88.4 °F (31.3 °C), low 49.8 °F (9.9 °C).
- 90 °F+ on average 36.9 days/year; 32 °F or lower on average 164 days/year.

Directions
- From I-5 (Redding): Hwy 44 east 48 mi to Hwy 89; follow Hwy 89 south 1 mi to north entrance.
- From I-5 (Red Bluff): Hwy 36 E 51 mi to Hwy 89; follow Hwy 89 north 6 mi to south entrance.
- Directions URL: http://www.nps.gov/lavo/planyourvisit/directions.htm

Operating hours
- Park open year-round, 24 hours daily.
- Road access limited approximately November–May due to snow.

Entrance fees (valid up to 7 consecutive days)
- Entrance – Private Vehicle: $30.00
- Entrance – Private Vehicle (winter discounted): $10.00
- Entrance – Motorcycle: $25.00
- Entrance – Motorcycle (winter discounted): $10.00
- Entrance – Per Person (foot/bicycle or non-commercial organized group): $15.00
- Entrance – Per Person (winter discounted): $10.00
- Entrance – Education/Academic Groups: $0.00 (fee waiver with approved application; apply at least 2 weeks prior)
- Commercial Entrance – Sedan: $25.00
- Commercial Entrance – Van: $50.00
- Commercial Entrance – Mini-bus: $60.00
- Commercial Entrance – Motor Coach: $150.00
Notes: Valid for up to 7 consecutive days for the same group. Commercial fees based on total seating capacity, regardless of passengers. Annual/lifetime passes not accepted for commercial entry. When entrance station is unstaffed, buy digital passes at recreation.gov.

Entrance pass
- Annual Entrance – Park: $55.00. Valid for 1 year from month of purchase at Lassen Volcanic NP, Crater Lake NP, Whiskeytown NRA, and Lava Beds NM. Admits one vehicle and occupants, or one motorcycle and riders, or pass holder plus 3 others on bicycle/foot.

Topics
- Arts; Explorers and Expeditions; Native American Heritage; Science, Technology and Innovation; Wars and Conflicts; Colonial/European Contact Conflicts; Westward Expansion; Women’s History.
