Tool `National Parks:getCampgrounds` with Parameter {'parkCode': 'lavo', 'limit': 50} on National Parks succeeded. Result (summarized from 26233 tokens): Lassen Volcanic National Park – Camping and Backcountry Summary (entries provided: 6 of 10)

Backcountry Camping in Lassen’s Wilderness (park code: lavo)
- Overview: Year-round backcountry overnight trips; no designated sites or amenities. Some areas closed to camping (near developed areas, water bodies, hydrothermal areas).
- Permits/Reservations: Wilderness Permit required for any overnight outside established campgrounds; obtain online only via recreation.gov before trip; 1 permit per trip; group size max 10; no permit quotas; carry a digital/printed copy; no check-in/out required.
- Fees: $6 nonrefundable administrative fee per permit + $5 per person per trip (no per-night fee).
- Key Regulations: Max 30 days per calendar year; pets not allowed; bicycles not allowed; hunting prohibited; firearms only per valid CA Concealed Weapons Permit; bear spray not permitted; bear-resistant containers required Apr 16–Nov 30; bury human waste in catholes; pack out TP/hygiene products and all trash/food; vehicles may be left in parking areas overnight for duration on permit; stock not allowed overnight; in winter when the park road is closed, camping allowed on/near the road.
- Access/Season: Year-round; access limited Nov–May due to deep snow.
- Weather: Very little summer precipitation; up to ~40 ft snowfall in winter; snow can linger into July–Aug; conditions vary with elevation.
- Location: 38050 Highway 36 East, Lassen Volcanic National Park, Mineral, CA 96063.
- Accessibility: No ADA facilities; primitive, uneven trails; OPDMDs not allowed in wilderness.
- Contacts: Email lavo_information@nps.gov. Info: nps.gov/lavo/planyourvisit/wilderness-permit-information.htm; Permits: recreation.gov/permits/4675334; Regulations: nps.gov/lavo/learn/management/backcountryregulations.htm.

Butte Lake Campground
- Location/Access: Remote NE corner; 6-mile Butte Lake Road south of Hwy 44; ~45 min from NW Entrance; elevation 6,100 ft.
- Reservations: Required for all sites all season; book up to 6 months ahead until arrival day; limited/no connectivity in park; staff/hosts don’t handle reservations. 9/3–10/14 only Loop B open; water off (no drinking water or flush toilets).
- Fees: Single campsite $22 (water off $15); Group $62 (water off $35); Stock corral $37.
- Sites/Types: 101 total; 6 group sites; 1 stock corral. No hookups.
- Amenities: Seasonal vault toilets; seasonal potable water; dump station; camp store; food storage lockers; trash/recycling. No showers.
- Regulations: Leashed pets permitted; drones prohibited; must occupy site upon payment; stays limited to 14 days per year; checkout 12 pm; quiet 10 pm–6 am; generators 8–10 am, 12–2 pm, 5–7 pm; wash dishes at campsite only; limited downed wood gathering (within 30 ft of road, <4" diameter); no chainsaws; fires only in grates; fully extinguish.
- Accessibility: Site A-6 ADA. RVs/trailers allowed; max length 35 ft; unpaved access road OK for all vehicles in good weather.
- Weather: Highs ~68–84°F; lows ~29–39°F; campground usually snow-free by June.
- Contacts/Links: Phone 530-595-6121; Email lavo_fees@nps.gov; Info: nps.gov/lavo/planyourvisit/butte-lake-campground.htm; Reservations: recreation.gov/camping/campgrounds/234156.

Juniper Lake Campground
- Status: Closed; work in progress to re-open.
- Location/Access: East shore of Juniper Lake; 13-mile paved/gravel road; elevation 6,792 ft.
- Reservations: Single sites are first-come, first-served only; group sites and stock corral by reservation.
- Fees: Single $12 (no water); Group $32 (tent-only; 10–15 people; up to 6 vehicles; includes 3 tables, 3 fire grates, 3 lockers); Stock corral $30 (max 10 people, 8 animals, 4 licensed vehicles including trailers; portable corrals not allowed except within designated enclosure).
- Sites/Types: 18 single FCFS; 2 group (reservable); 1 stock corral (reservable).
- Amenities: No drinking water; vault toilets (seasonal); food storage lockers; trash/recycling. No showers.
- Accessibility: Mostly flat s
