Images (selection of themes and examples)
- Canopy and groves, nurse logs, fire-scarred giants, and redwood resprouting (e.g., Fish-eye view of Redwood canopy; How Tall is that Redwood?; Fire scarred giants; Redwoods Resprouting).
- Popular trails and features: Trillium Falls; Trillium Falls Trail; Lady Bird Johnson Grove footbridge; Stout Grove; Tall Trees Grove.
- Coastline and beaches: Enderts Beach; Coastline at Redwood National Park; Incoming Tide; tide pooling; whale-watching overlooks.
- Fern Canyon highlight.
- Visitor experience: Scenic driving on Howland Hill Road; ranger programs; Junior Ranger; planning and family walks.
- General note: Over 40 miles of coastline and 100+ miles of trails depicted across images.
- Image credits primarily NPS photographers (e.g., Steve Olson, John Chao).
Tool `National Parks:getCampgrounds` with Parameter {'parkCode': 'redw', 'limit': 50} on National Parks succeeded. Result (summarized from 8978 tokens): Redwood National and State Parks (parkCode: redw) — Developed Campgrounds (4 total)

General reservations, fees, and contacts
- Reservations: Reserve California (https://www.reservecalifornia.com/Web/ | 1-800-444-7275). Reservations and questions are handled via Reserve California.
- Fees (per night): Standard $35; CA State Parks Disabled Discount $17.50; CA State Parks Distinguished Veterans $0; Federal “America the Beautiful” Senior or Access $17.50. Passes must be presented at check-in. Federal Annual Passholders pay the standard fee.
- General info email: redw_information@nps.gov

1) Elk Prairie Campground (Prairie Creek Redwoods State Park)
- Highlights: Ancient coast redwoods, frequent Roosevelt elk and black‑tailed deer, access to 70+ miles of hiking/biking, seasonal ranger-led programs; cabins available. In the heart of Prairie Creek Redwoods SP, ~6 miles north of Orick, CA.
- Location: 41.35982485324314, -124.02943276711778; mailing city Crescent City, CA 95531
- Operating: Open year-round; reservations essential May–Oct.
- Sites: 75 total; 75 reservable; 0 first-come. Types: tent-only 21; RV-only 1; other 4; no group/horse/electric.
- Amenities: Trash/recycling; flush toilets (year-round); hot showers (free, year-round); potable water (year-round); dump station; internet; cell service; laundry; amphitheater; camp store; staff/host onsite; ice and firewood for sale; food storage lockers.
- Accessibility/RVs: ADA trail to amphitheater; level aggregate pads. RVs allowed (max 27 ft); trailers allowed (max 24 ft). Access roads paved; all vehicles OK. Four ADA-accessible cabins available.
- Regulations: “Hike and Bike” sites are for hikers/bicyclists only; no vehicle arrivals may use them.
- Info: https://www.nps.gov/redw/planyourvisit/elk-prairie-campground.htm

2) Gold Bluffs Beach Campground (Prairie Creek Redwoods State Park – coast, southern parks)
- Highlights: Wild Pacific coastline, Roosevelt elk, secluded beach, Fern Canyon access, 70 miles of hiking/biking. Access via narrow, single‑lane dirt road; RVs not advised; trailers prohibited.
- Location: 41.38221738914677, -124.0698821873994; Orick, CA 95555
- Operating: Open year-round; winter access may be limited due to road conditions.
- Sites: 26 total; 26 reservable; 0 first-come. No designated tent-only/RV-only/other counts; no electric.
- Amenities: Trash/recycling; flush toilets (year-round); hot showers (free, year-round); potable water (year-round); dump station; internet; cell service; laundry; amphitheater; camp store; staff/host onsite; ice and firewood for sale; food storage lockers.
- Accessibility/RVs: Beach wheelchairs available. RVs allowed (max 24 ft) but not advised; trailers not allowed. Unpaved road; all vehicles OK in good weather. No ADA-designated sites.
- Regulations: “Hike and Bike” backcountry site for hikers/bicyclists only; minimum 5‑mile hike or 10‑mile ride; free backcountry permit required; no motorized vehicle arrivals allowed at hike & bike sites.
- Info: https://www.nps.gov/redw/planyourvisit/gold-bluffs-beach-campground.htm

3) Jedediah Smith Campground (Jedediah Smith Redwoods State Park)
- Highlights: Old-growth redwood grove on the Smith River; hiking, swimming, fishing; seasonal campfire programs; cabins available. Northern-most campground in the parks; operated by CA State Parks.
- Location: 41.79572647634519, -124.08644744393519; Crescent City, CA 95531
- Operating: Open year-round.
- Sites: 86 total; 86 reservable; 0 first-come. Types: tent-only 22; RV-only 1; other 4; no group/horse/electric.
- Amenities: Trash/recycling; flush toilets (year-round); showers (coin‑operated, year‑round); potable water (year‑round); dump station; internet; cell service; laundry; amphitheater; camp store; staff/host onsite; ice and firewood for sale; food storage lockers.
- Accessibility/RVs: RVs allowed (max 25 ft); trailers allowed (max 21 ft). Paved roads; all vehicles OK. Four ADA-accessible cabins available.
- Info: https://www.nps.gov/redw
