Tool `National Parks:getParkDetails` with Parameter {'parkCode': 'pinn'} on National Parks succeeded. Result (summarized from 2983 tokens): Pinnacles National Park (code: pinn)
- Website: https://www.nps.gov/pinn/index.htm
- Designation: National Park
- State: CA

Overview
- Formed ~23 million years ago by volcanic eruptions, leaving rocky spires and deep canyons.
- Environments include chaparral, oak woodlands, and cool, shaded canyon floors.

Weather
- Mediterranean climate; park lies several miles inland from the Pacific.
- Summers: hot and dry, often above 100°F.
- Winters: milder, highs in the 60s with moderate precipitation.
- Large day–night temperature swings year-round.

Getting There
- West entrance: via Hwy 101 → City of Soledad → Hwy 146.
- East entrance: via Hwy 25 (through Hollister from the north; from the south via King City → Bitter Water Rd/G-13).
- Important: No through road between east and west entrances.
- Directions: http://www.nps.gov/pinn/planyourvisit/directions.htm

Location
- Coordinates: 36.49029208, -121.1813607
- Address: 5000 East Entrance Road, Paicines, CA 95043

Contacts
- Phone (voice): 831-389-4486
- Fax: 831-389-4288
- Email: pinn_visitor_information@nps.gov (include visit dates/season if applicable; typical reply within one week). For volunteer opportunities: pinn_volunteer@nps.gov

Entrance Fees (valid 1–7 days unless noted)
- Private vehicle: $30 (all occupants, East and West Entrances)
- Motorcycle: $25 (all riders)
- Per Person (on foot/bicycle): $15
- Non-commercial groups (16+ capacity): $15 per person, up to the maximums used for comparable commercial vehicles ($40 or $100). Exemptions: age 15 and under, valid passholders, and hired drivers for transportation only.
- Commercial tours (price based on seating capacity, not passenger count; passes/ages don’t affect price):
  - Sedan (1–6 seats): $30
  - Van (7–15 seats): $40
  - Mini-bus (16–25 seats): $40
  - Motor coach (26+ seats): $100
- Educational/Academic groups: $0 with approved Educational Fee Waiver (otherwise see large/commercial group fees)

Entrance Passes
- Pinnacles Annual Pass: $55; valid 12 months from purchase. Covers the signee and accompanying passengers in a single, non-commercial vehicle. Available at entrance stations.

Operating Hours
- East Side Entrance: Open 24/7 year-round, including holidays.
- West Side Entrance: Daily 7:30 AM–8:00 PM. One-lane, narrow, winding road; oversize vehicles should use the east entrance. Access to trails including Prewett Point, Balconies, and Juniper Canyon.

Activities
- Astronomy, Stargazing
- Biking, Road Biking
- Camping (Car/Front Country, Group, RV)
- Caving
- Climbing, Rock Climbing
- Food: Picnicking
- Hands-On: Citizen Science, Volunteer Vacation
- Hiking (Backcountry, Front-Country)
- Junior Ranger Program
- Wildlife Watching, Birdwatching
- Park Film
- Shopping: Bookstore/Park Store, Gift Shop/Souvenirs

Topics (highlights)
- History & Culture: Architecture/Building; Archeology; Colonization/Settlement; Dams; Engineering; Enslavement; Explorers/Expeditions; Farming/Agriculture; Ranches; Great Depression; Hispanic/Latino American Heritage; Industry & Mining; Immigration & Migrations; Military/US Army; Native American Heritage; Presidents; Religion/Spirituality & Missions; Schools/Education; Science/Technology/Innovation; Social Movements & Conservation Movement; Transportation (Bridges, Roads/Highways, Tunnels); Tragic Events (Catastrophic Fires, Floods); Wars & Conflicts (Spanish-American War, Cold War); Westward Expansion (Homesteading, The Gold Rush).
- Natural Features & Processes: Ancient Seas; Animals (Birds, Wild Cats, Fish, Tortoises/Turtles, Wolves); Caves/Caverns/Karst; Canyons; Climate Change; Fire; Foothills/Plains/Valleys; Forests/Woodlands (Coniferous, Deciduous); Fossils/Paleontology; Geology & Mineral Deposits; Groundwater (Aquifers, Freshwater Springs); Grasslands/Meadows; Mountains; Natural Sounds; Night Sky/Astronomy; River/Riparian; Rock Landscapes/Features; Scenic Views; Thickets/Shrublands; Trails; Unique/Rare/Endangered Species; Volcanoes; Watersheds/Headwaters; Waterfalls; Wetlands
Tool `National Parks:getCampgrounds` with Parameter {'parkCode': 'pinn', 'limit': 50} on National Parks succeeded. Result (summarized from 2723 tokens): - Name: Pinnacles Campground (parkCode: pinn); operator: Pinnacles Recreation Company
- Location: 2400 HWY 146, Paicines, CA 95043; latitude 36.4898445959, longitude -121.148968014; paved access roads (all vehicles OK)
- Overview: Tent, group, RV sites, and tent cabins (some with electricity). Each tent and group site has a picnic table and fire ring. Most RV sites have electrical hookups and share community tables and barbecue pits. Tent cabins sleep up to 4. Water spigots throughout. Oak trees provide shade at many sites. Showers and a dump station available. Pets allowed in campground (not on trails). Swimming pool typically open mid-April through end of September (weather dependent).
- Reservations: All sites reservable (no first-come). Tent & RV sites bookable up to 6 months in advance; group sites up to 12 months. Reserve via Recreation.gov (https://www.recreation.gov/camping/campgrounds/234015) or call 877-444-6777. Info: visitpinnacles.com; campground store: 831-200-1722
- Operating hours: Open all day, daily
- Fees (per night):
  - Tent Site: $43.00 (up to 6 people, 2 vehicles)
  - RV Site: $59.00 (60A, 30A 240v, and 7.5A 110v outlets)
  - Group Site: $110.00 (max 10 people; reserve 6–12 months ahead)
  - Tent Cabin Electric: $139.00
  - Tent Cabin Nonelectric: $129.00
- Capacity and site inventory:
  - Total sites: 134; reservable: 134; first-come: 0
  - Breakdown: tent-only 83; group 21; RV-only 30; electrical hookups 30; horse/walk-in/other: 0
- Regulations:
  - Max 6 people per tent site; max 2 tents per tent site
  - Max 2 cars per camping site
  - Follow seasonal fire restrictions
- Amenities:
  - Trash/recycling; toilets (flush, composting, and portable, year-round)
  - Potable water (year-round)
  - Showers (hot, coin-operated, year-round)
  - Internet connectivity; cell phone reception
  - Laundry; amphitheater; dump station
  - Camp store; staff/volunteer host onsite
  - Ice and firewood for sale; food storage lockers
- Accessibility:
  - Campsites on mostly compact dirt; some loose soil/uneven; roads paved, parking spurs gravel
  - ADA info: flush toilets, potable water, showers, on-site general store; pool open April–September (weather permitting)
  - RVs allowed (max length 90 ft); trailers allowed (max length 45 ft)
- Weather: Park has a microclimate; conditions can differ from nearby towns. Check the park/campground website for the most accurate forecast
- Contacts and links:
  - Info/concerns: 831-200-1722; website: https://www.visitpinnacles.com/
  - Reservations: 877-444-6777; https://www.recreation.gov/camping/campgrounds/234015
