Tool `National Parks:getCampgrounds` with Parameter {'parkCode': 'chis', 'limit': 50} on National Parks succeeded. Result (summarized from 18236 tokens): Channel Islands National Park – Camping Summary (parkCode: chis)

Park-wide essentials
- Access: Boat-in only; no roads. All sites are walk-in from landings. No RVs or trailers.
- Reservations: Required for all camping; no first-come options. No entrance fees. Reserve via recreation.gov or 877-444-6777.
- Typical fee: $15 per site per night (except Santa Rosa backcountry beaches: $10).
- Weather: Expect wind, sun exposure, and fog any season; bring sturdy, low-profile tents and extra supplies in case seas delay pickup. Current conditions: http://channelislands.noaa.gov/news/kiosk.html
- Accessibility: Most locations are not accessible for wheelchairs or limited mobility due to boat transport, steep climbs, and rugged terrain.
- Regulations and policies: http://www.nps.gov/chis/learn/management/lawsandpolicies.htm
- Park contacts: 805-658-5730; chis_information@nps.gov

Campgrounds

1) Anacapa Island Campground (Anacapa Island, CA)
- Sites/fees: 7 primitive tent-only, boat/walk-in sites; $15/site/night. Six sites cover up to 4 people; one site covers up to 6.
- Open: Year-round.
- Facilities: Picnic table, food storage box, pit toilet; no water.
- Access: ~0.5 mile from landing, includes 157 stairs.
- Advisory: Western gull nesting Apr–mid-Aug brings rookery conditions (guano, odor, noise, carcasses, protective birds).
- Accessibility: Not accessible for wheelchairs/limited mobility.

2) San Miguel Island Campground (San Miguel Island, CA)
- Sites/fees: 9 primitive tent-only, boat/walk-in sites; $15/site/night (covers up to 4).
- Open: Year-round.
- Facilities: Wind shelter, picnic table, food storage box, pit toilet; no water.
- Access: ~1 mile from landing; steep canyon with ~400 ft climb.
- Accessibility: Not accessible for wheelchairs/limited mobility.

3) Santa Barbara Island Campground (Santa Barbara Island, CA)
- Sites/fees: Primitive tent-only, boat/walk-in; description notes 7 sites; fee $15/site/night (covers up to 4). Dataset lists 10 tent-only sites.
- Open: Year-round.
- Facilities: Picnic table, food storage box, pit toilet; no water.
- Access: ~0.25 mile from landing; steep climb.
- Accessibility: Not accessible for wheelchairs/limited mobility.

4) Santa Cruz Island Del Norte Backcountry Campground (Santa Cruz Island, CA)
- Sites/fees: 4 primitive tent-only sites (4 persons/site); $15/site/night. Backcountry camping allowed only here on Santa Cruz Island.
- Open: Year-round.
- Facilities: Picnic table, food storage box, pit-style toilet (bring your own toilet paper); no water.
- Access: Hike-in only: 3.5 miles from Prisoners Harbor or 12 miles from Scorpion Anchorage; camp only within designated sites.
- Backcountry regulations (highlights): Store all food in animal/bird-proof containers; pack out all trash; no fires. Strain food from gray water and pack out particles; scatter gray water 200 ft from water/camps; minimize soap and rinse 200 ft from water sources; do not damage live trees/plants.

5) Santa Cruz Island Scorpion Canyon Campground (Santa Cruz Island, CA)
- Sites/fees: 25 individual tent-only sites at $15/site/night (up to 6 people) and 6 group sites at $40/site/night (up to 15 people).
- Open: Year-round.
- Facilities: Picnic tables, food storage boxes, pit toilets; potable water available year-round.
- Access: ~0.5 mile from landing.
- Accessibility: Limited. For boat accessibility details, contact Island Packers at 805-642-1393; for on-island transport info, call 805-658-5730.

6) Santa Rosa Island Backcountry Beach Camping (Santa Rosa Island, CA)
- Season: Aug 15–Dec 31 only. Closed Jan 1–Aug 14 to protect pupping seals/sea lions and nesting seabirds.
- Open areas:
  - Aug 15–Sep 15: Southeast quadrant beaches (East Point to South Point) open to camping (boaters, kayakers, backpackers).
  - Sep 16–Dec 31: Southeast, Southwest, and Northwest quadrant beaches open. Beaches around Sandy Point, at Lobo Canyon, and some Northeast beaches (between Carrington…) have restrictions; consult current maps/not
