- programs.firefox.darwinDefaultsId: ID for macOS (Darwin) defaults to set policies.
- programs.firefox.finalPackage: Resulting Firefox package.
- programs.firefox.languagePacks: Language packs to install. Codes at https://releases.mozilla.org/pub/firefox/releases/${version}/linux-x86_64/xpi/ (replace ${version}).
- programs.firefox.nativeMessagingHosts: Additional packages providing native messaging hosts for extensions.
- programs.firefox.pkcs11Modules: Additional packages to load as PKCS #11 modules.
- programs.firefox.policies: Firefox policies (see list of policies).
- programs.firefox.profiles: Attribute set of Firefox profiles.
  - profiles.<name>.bookmarks: Declarative bookmarks.
    - configFile: File defining custom bookmarks.
    - force: Force override existing custom bookmarks.
    - meta.maintainers: List of maintainers (define at most once per module).
    - settings: Custom bookmarks.
  - profiles.<name>.containers: Container configurations (see Multi-Account Containers).
    - <name>.color: Container color.
    - <name>.icon: Container icon.
    - <name>.id: Unique numeric ID per container in this profile.
    - <name>.name: Container name (e.g., shopping).
    - containersForce: Force replace existing container configuration. Recommended (Firefox replaces the symlink each launch) but existing config will be lost.
  - profiles.<name>.extensions: Install/configure extensions.
    - packages: List of add-on packages to install for this profile. Some pre-packaged add-ons are available from NUR.
    - exactPermissions: If enabled, extensions.settings.<extensionID>.permissions must exactly match permissions requested by the extension.
    - exhaustivePermissions: If enabled, user must authorize requested permissions for all extensions from packages.
    - force: Override all previous Firefox settings.
    - settings: Options per extension; keys are the extension ID or its UUID in {}.
      - <name>.force: Force override of existing extension configuration.
      - <name>.permissions: Allowed permissions (see MDN WebExtensions manifest permissions).
      - <name>.settings: JSON-formatted options.
  - profiles.<name>.extraConfig: Extra preferences to append to user.js.
  - profiles.<name>.id: Unique profile ID (number) per profile.
  - profiles.<name>.isDefault: Whether this is the default profile.
  - profiles.<name>.name: Profile name.
  - profiles.<name>.path: Profile path.
  - profiles.<name>.preConfig: Extra preferences to add to user.js before settings.
  - profiles.<name>.search: Declarative search engine configuration.
    - default: Default engine for address bar and search bar.
    - engines: Engine configurations; entries with only metaData are treated as built-in.
    - force: Force replace existing search configuration. Recommended (Firefox replaces the symlink each launch) but existing config will be lost.
    - meta.maintainers: List of maintainers (define at most once per module).
    - order: Order of search engines; others appear afterward in unspecified order.
    - privateDefault: Default engine in Private Browsing.
  - profiles.<name>.settings: Firefox preferences (attribute set).
  - profiles.<name>.userChrome: Custom user chrome CSS.
  - profiles.<name>.userContent: Custom user content CSS.
- programs.firefoxpwa.enable: Enable Progressive Web Apps for Firefox.
- programs.firefoxpwa.package: firefoxpwa package to use.
