Tool `NixOS:home_manager_options_by_prefix` with Parameter {'option_prefix': 'programs.firefox'} on NixOS succeeded. Result (summarized from 1531 tokens): Home Manager options for programs.firefox (summary)

Top-level
- programs.firefox.enable: Enable Firefox.
- programs.firefox.package: Firefox package to use. For stateVersion ≥ 19.09 use a wrapped package; earlier versions use unwrapped. Set to null to disable installing.
- programs.firefox.finalPackage: Resulting/wrapped Firefox package.
- programs.firefox.languagePacks: Language packs to install. Codes available at https://releases.mozilla.org/pub/firefox/releases/${version}/linux-x86_64/xpi/ (replace ${version}).
- programs.firefox.nativeMessagingHosts: Extra packages providing native messaging hosts for extensions.
- programs.firefox.pkcs11Modules: Extra packages loaded as PKCS #11 modules.
- programs.firefox.policies: Firefox enterprise policies (see policy list).
- programs.firefox.enableGnomeExtensions: Enable GNOME Shell native host connector. Also set NixOS option services.gnome.gnome-browser-connector.enable = true.
- programs.firefox.darwinDefaultsId: ID used to set policies via macOS (Darwin) defaults.

Profiles (programs.firefox.profiles)
- programs.firefox.profiles: Attrset of profiles.
- profiles.<name>.id: Unique numeric profile ID (per profile).
- profiles.<name>.name: Profile name.
- profiles.<name>.path: Profile path.
- profiles.<name>.isDefault: Whether this is the default profile.
- profiles.<name>.settings: Attrset of Firefox prefs (about:config style).
- profiles.<name>.preConfig: Extra preferences appended to user.js before settings.
- profiles.<name>.extraConfig: Extra preferences appended to user.js after settings.
- profiles.<name>.userChrome: Custom userChrome.css.
- profiles.<name>.userContent: Custom userContent.css.

Bookmarks (profiles.<name>.bookmarks)
- bookmarks: Declarative bookmarks.
- bookmarks.settings: Custom bookmarks.
- bookmarks.configFile: Path to custom bookmarks definition file.
- bookmarks.force: Force override of existing custom bookmarks.
- bookmarks.meta.maintainers: List of maintainers (define at most once per module).

Containers (profiles.<name>.containers)
- containers: Attrset of container configs (Multi-Account Containers).
- containers.<name>.name: Container name (e.g., shopping).
- containers.<name>.color: Container color.
- containers.<name>.icon: Container icon.
- containers.<name>.id: Unique numeric container ID (per container in this profile).
- containersForce: Force replace the existing containers config. Recommended (Firefox replaces the symlink on each launch), but you’ll lose existing configuration when enabled.

Extensions (profiles.<name>.extensions)
- extensions: Submodule for installing/configuring extensions.
- extensions.packages: List of add-on packages to install for this profile (some available via NUR).
- extensions.force: Override all previous Firefox extension settings.
- extensions.settings: Attrset keyed by extension ID or UUID in {braces}; per-extension options:
  - settings.<ext>.settings: JSON-formatted options for the extension.
  - settings.<ext>.permissions: Allowed permissions for the extension (see MDN WebExtensions permissions).
  - settings.<ext>.force: Force override any existing configuration for this extension.
- extensions.exactPermissions: If enabled, extensions.settings.<ext>.permissions must exactly match the extension’s requested permissions.
- extensions.exhaustivePermissions: If enabled, the user must authorize requested permissions for all extensions from extensions.packages in extensions.settings.<ext> (per the referenced paths).

Search (profiles.<name>.search)
- search: Declarative search engine configuration.
- search.default: Default search engine for address/search bar.
- search.privateDefault: Default search engine for Private Browsing.
- search.engines: Attrset of engine configs; engines with only metaData are treated as built-in.
- search.order: Ordering of engines; unspecified engines follow in unspecified order.
- search.force: Force replace search configuration. Recommended (Firefox replaces the symlink on each lau
