- programs.firefox.enable (boolean): Enable the Firefox web browser.
- programs.firefox.package (package): Which Firefox package to use.
- programs.firefox.wrapperConfig (attr set): Arguments passed to the Firefox wrapper.
- programs.firefox.autoConfig (string; lines joined with “\n”): AutoConfig to set/lock prefs not covered by policies.json on Mac/Linux; can enforce defaults or lock prefs. More info: https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/customizing-firefox-using-autoconfig
- programs.firefox.autoConfigFiles (list of absolute path): Additional AutoConfig files; concatenated and appended to autoConfig.
- programs.firefox.preferences (attr set of boolean | signed int | string): about:config preferences. Some may be more ergonomically set via policies. See “allowed preferences.” Note: When used, Firefox shows “Your browser is managed by your organization” because NixOS enforces these settings (not an external takeover unless they control your NixOS config).
- programs.firefox.policies (JSON value): Mozilla enterprise policies to install (see Mozilla documentation). Can declaratively install extensions via ExtensionSettings policy. Same “managed by your organization” note as above.
