Native messaging host toggles (booleans):
- programs.firefox.nativeMessagingHosts.browserpass: Enable Browserpass support.
- programs.firefox.nativeMessagingHosts.bukubrow: Enable Bukubrow support.
- programs.firefox.nativeMessagingHosts.euwebid: Enable Web eID support.
- programs.firefox.nativeMessagingHosts.ff2mpv: Enable ff2mpv support.
- programs.firefox.nativeMessagingHosts.fxCast: Enable fx_cast support.
- programs.firefox.nativeMessagingHosts.gsconnect: Enable GSConnect support.
- programs.firefox.nativeMessagingHosts.jabref: Enable JabRef support.
- programs.firefox.nativeMessagingHosts.passff: Enable PassFF support.
- programs.firefox.nativeMessagingHosts.tridactyl: Enable Tridactyl support.

Services:
- services.firefox-syncserver.enable (boolean): Enable Firefox Sync storage service. By default not useful unless you configure at least one service and one node in MySQL, e.g.:
  - INSERT INTO services (id, service, pattern) VALUES ('1','sync-1.5','{node}/1.5/{uid}');
  - INSERT INTO nodes (id, service, node, available, current_load, capacity, downed, backoff) VALUES ('1','1','https://mydomain.tld','1','0','10','0','0');
  services.firefox-syncserver.singleNode.enable performs this automatically when enabled.
- services.gokapi.enable (boolean): Enable Gokapi, a lightweight self-hosted Firefox Send alternative without public upload.
